diff --git a/tests/host-transfer-notes.md b/tests/host-transfer-notes.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..ab7eb083
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/host-transfer-notes.md
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# Host transfer corrections
+
+R/W retain the port 161 host service and use source -> destination syntax.
+
+Examples:
+
+    R FILE.TXT
+    W FILE.TXT
+    R TEST.TXT B3:TEST2.TXT
+    R TEST.TXT B3:
+    W B3:TEST.TXT TEST2.TXT
+
+Host operands are flat 8.3 filenames. Guest operands accept a drive A-P and
+optional user 0-15. Omitted locations use the current drive/user; omitted
+destination names retain the source name. Explicit user selection is restored
+on all ordinary return paths. H: mapping and host listing are deferred.
+
+/VER, /H and /HELP are exact case-insensitive queries, recognized before any
+file operations. The commands currently identify as 1.0 (003-dev).
+
+ Host reads now
+return 0 for a record, 1 for normal EOF, and FF for error. Install the rebuilt R
+with the rebuilt emulator: older emulators return FF at normal host EOF, which
+new R correctly treats as an error under the revised contract. Old R continues
+to work with the new emulator but cannot distinguish EOF from read failure.
+
+Corrections: persistent text EOF, checked read/close results, cleared closed
+handles, cleanup before replacing a stream, atomic exclusive creation when
+SIMBDOS_NO_OVERWRITE is enabled, and lowercase filename documentation.
+
+Validation: cpmsim builds; R and W assemble; test_host_transfer.py exercises
+text EOF across records, binary Ctrl-Z preservation, partial-record padding,
+normal EOF versus injected read error, injected close failure, repeated close,
+I/O after close, missing files, and both overwrite configurations.
+Guest runtime integration has not been exercised.
+
+Still existing behavior: default overwrites are destructive, failed transfers
+can leave partial destinations, and extension-selected text mode is implicit.
+Proposed next steps: explicit text/binary mode; overwrite confirmation with a
+force option; temporary destination plus rename on success; configurable host transfer directory; wildcard batches.
+MOUNT should reuse the existing disk swap implementation after its interface
+and guest reset requirements have been inspected. General host execution is
+out of scope.
+
+Syntax validation: test_rw_transfers.py executes assembled commands on the Z80
+core with the real host service and a BDOS fixture, covering renamed imports
+and exports, defaults, DU selection, invalid syntax, data and user restoration
+on success and injected failure. Full guest OS integration remains untested.
+
+Host operands retain their typed case; guest operands and inherited import
+names are uppercase. Text-extension recognition is case-insensitive. An omitted
+W destination inherits the normalized uppercase CP/M name. Mixed-case use
+requires a CCP that preserves command tails; older CCPs cannot recover typed
+spelling. Case-distinct import probes skip on case-insensitive volumes.
